ID: vr-17
Title: Deferred animation-ready custom avatar asset
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/16

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: A reviewed neutral identity with a tested, editable facial asset.
Dependencies: vr-16

Purpose:
DEFERRED until explicit owner resumption and vr-16's positive feasibility gate.
Use the approved sculpt as a shape source, not a promise that an arbitrary
static GLB can be automatically repaired into a faithful animated character.
Produce an asset suitable for actual facial deformation and local rendering.

Tasks:
[ ] 17.1 Freeze the approved identity reference and working-source version;
    retain the original sculpt and before/after comparison views.
[ ] 17.2 Build or qualify animation-suitable face topology and separate the
    skin, hair and controllable eyes where needed. Preserve the approved
    silhouette while measuring the cost of simplification; do not decimate
    mouth/eyelid contacts blindly to reach an arbitrary triangle number.
[ ] 17.3 Correct supported proportions and eye/lip placement against the
    approved views. Re-review meaningful changes before texturing or rigging.
[ ] 17.4 Build usable eyelids, eyeballs, lip boundaries and mouth interior.
    Add teeth/tongue only if the selected articulation route requires them;
    explicitly document omissions and what cannot be animated correctly.
[ ] 17.5 Create a consistent UV/material route for skin, lips, brows, eyes and
    hair. Author or lawfully obtain required textures; document color space,
    opacity, normal/tangent conventions and actual shader requirements.
[ ] 17.6 Create documented facial morphs or a facial rig with named controls,
    ranges and neutral values for jaw, lip closure/pucker/spread and eyelids,
    plus only the supported expression controls. Do not equate names with
    anatomically or phonetically valid behavior.
[ ] 17.7 Validate isolated and combined extremes: bilabial closure, jaw-open
    with lip shapes, blink/gaze coverage, expression combinations, finite
    geometry, unwanted motion and return to the exact neutral state.
[ ] 17.8 Define full-bust and head/lower-neck geometry groups or derived LODs.
    Specify how crop boundaries, hair and polygon contours retain intended
    behavior across all orientations, without adding a full-body scope.
[ ] 17.9 Export an editable source and pinned GLB package with control manifest,
    coordinate/scale/material contract and hashes. Verify exported data
    independently rather than trusting a screenshot or filename extension.

Acceptance criteria:
vr-16 has a positive go and rights/identity prerequisites are resolved.
The neutral likeness has an explicit owner review outcome; no silent identity
drift during optimization. Geometry, eyes, mouth and controls are actually
editable and functional, not a static sculpt with invented rig metadata.
Exporter/import inspection agrees on transforms, morph names/ranges, materials,
required images and reset behavior. Missing/external/unsupported assets fail
explicitly. Realism and expression accuracy remain separately qualified.
No rights-restricted asset or private reference is published automatically.

Completion evidence:
Planning only; asset preparation, rigging and exports have NOT STARTED.
The inspected candidate is a dense connected static sculpt, not this milestone.
No approved retopology, facial controls, textures, editable source or replacement
runtime model exists from this plan.

Completion log:
2026-11-19 - Recorded the deferred asset work after the owner's parking decision.
Depends on vr-16; no modeling, tooling install or asset redistribution performed.
